How to build:

1) Place files like this in your buildroot directory

buildroot/
├── board/
│   └── insa/
│       └── sse/
│           ├── stm32mp151.dtsi    
│           └── stm32mp157c-dk2.dts  
├── configs/
│   └── insa_defconfig              
└── package/
    └── ultrasound/   

2) In buildroot/ :
    $ make insa_defconfig
    $ make 
    $ sudo dd if=./output/images/sdcard.img of=/dev/<YOUR_SD_CARD> status=progress bs=1M oflag=sync

   On the card : 
    $ passwd root
    $ sed -i 's/^#\?PermitRscp driver_lcd.py 192.168.1.139:/tmpootLogin.*/PermitRootLogin yes/' /etc/ssh/sshd_config
    $ pidof sshd
    $ kill <PID_OF_SSHD>

How to connect to the card:

1) UART connection (shell):
    $ picocom -b 115200 /dev/ttyACM0    (Might need to use sudo if permission denied)

2) SSH connection (file transfer)
    $ scp driver_lcd.py <IP_OF_THE_CARD>:/tmp

How to use the driver :

1) Basic 
    Access the shell of the card
    $ python3 read.py

2) Socket
    Find the card's IP 
    On the card's shell:   
        $ python3 socket_sender.py
    On the PC's shell: 
        $ python3 socket_receiver.py <CARD'S IP> 300

3) Web server

    On the card :
        Put this file structure : 
        ├── serveurFlask.py
        └── templates/
            └── index.html
        
        $ python3 serveurFlask.py

    On the computer :
        Connect to http://<CARD's IP>:5000/ via any web browser


